<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mithridates II of Parthia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 91 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mithridates II was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthian Empire</a> from about 124 to 91 BCE. He restored Parthian power after the defeats of his predecessors by the Saka, subdued the nomads and settled many of them in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sistan">Sakastan</a>, and pushed the western frontier to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a>. He received an embassy from Han <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, took the title King of Kings and made the first Parthian agreement with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulla">Sulla</a>, in about 96 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mithridates-ii-of-parthia.jpg" alt="Mithridates II of Parthia" width="320" height="304" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coin_of_Mithridates_II_of_Parthia,_Ray_mint.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Under <b>Mithridates II</b> (r. c. 124–91 BCE) Parthia reached the Euphrates and established the first diplomatic contacts with Rome, which would become its great western rival.</blockquote><a href="/empire/parthian-empire">Parthian Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Parthian kings fought them for decades: Phraates II was killed in battle against them in about 127 BCE, and <b>Mithridates II</b> subdued them and appears to have settled them in Sakastan by around 100 BCE.</blockquote><a href="/empire/saka">Saka · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Nisa, in what is now <a href="/countries/turkmenistan">Turkmenistan</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ctesiphon">Ctesiphon</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/iraq">Iraq</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=37.95,58.21&amp;year=-101" aria-label="Nisa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6001 799 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Mithridates II of Parthia"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6451 1069h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6451 1069h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=37.95,58.21&amp;year=-101">What was here in 101 BCE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
